From: BananaDS <bananads@localhost>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 08:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ARMJIT_Memory: map the DTCM itself into fastmem

MapAtAddress and Mapping::Unmap leave a hole for the DTCM in the regions it overlaps (main RAM's mirrors). The
same code ran for the DTCM's own region, where the hole is all of it: nothing was mapped, but the pages were
marked mapped, so the access faulted again and was rewritten to the slow path. Every DTCM access stayed a slow
call: most games keep the ARM9's stack there. HeartGold's overworld: ~21,000 slow calls a frame (reads, writes,
LDM and STM of the stack), gone; on the RG DS Plus at 1104 MHz, 2x, 49.6 -> 60.2 fps; 1x at 1992 MHz 75.9 -> 88.3.
The same frames. A DTCM smaller than a host page stays on the slow path.
---
--- a/src/ARMJIT_Memory.cpp
+++ b/src/ARMJIT_Memory.cpp
@@ -471,7 +471,9 @@
 
 #ifndef __SWITCH__
     u32 dtcmEnd = dtcmStart + dtcmSize;
+    // (the hole is for the regions the DTCM overlaps; the DTCM's own mapping is all of it)
     if (Num == 0
+        && region != memregion_DTCM
         && dtcmEnd >= Addr
         && dtcmStart < Addr + Size)
     {
@@ -656,7 +658,13 @@
     u32 dtcmSize = ~NDS.ARM9.DTCMMask + 1;
     u32 dtcmEnd = dtcmStart + dtcmSize;
 #ifndef __SWITCH__
+    // (the DTCM's own mapping is all of it: with the hole logic it mapped nothing, but marked its pages mapped, so
+    // the access faulted again and was rewritten to the slow path, and every DTCM access, the ARM9's stack in most
+    // games, stayed there)
+    if (region == memregion_DTCM && mirrorSize < PageSize)
+        return false;
     if (num == 0
+        && region != memregion_DTCM
         && dtcmEnd >= mirrorStart
         && dtcmStart < mirrorStart + mirrorSize)
     {
